      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{5x+12}-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{5x+12}-3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{5x+12}-3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{5x+12} & =3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{5x+12})^{3} & ={3}^{3} \\\\ 5x+12 & =27 \\\\ 5x & =15 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=3.$",
